=The following have already expired:

{{ $json.expired_txt }}

Depending on what these are, you may currently be uninsured, or unable to legally carry out certain work. Worth stopping to check before the next job rather than after.

{{ $json.counts.week ? 'Also expiring within 7 days:\n' + $json.week_txt : '' }}

This is a reminder from your own records — it isn't legal or insurance advice. Confirm with your broker or trade body.

={{ $json.counts.week ? 'WITHIN 7 DAYS — sort this week:
' + $json.week_txt + '
' : '' }}
{{ $json.counts.month ? 'Within 30 days:
' + $json.month_txt + '
' : '' }}
{{ $json.isMonday && $json.counts.quarter ? 'On the horizon (90 days):
' + $json.quarter_txt : '' }}

Renewals are cheaper and calmer when they're not urgent. Starting a public liability renewal 30 days out usually gets a better quote than doing it the week it lapses.
